Platform: Nova Lake NPU (60xx IP) under kernel 6.19 with intel_vpu loaded but
no NPU firmware, so the probe fails: the PCI function has no driver and no
accel node. NPU-only fixture.

Sources:
- 0x8086 0xd71d NPU: drivers/accel/ivpu/ivpu_drv.h (PCI_DEVICE_ID_NVL, 60xx IP);
  class 0x1200 per intel-device-plugins' NFD rule (deployments/nfd/overlays/
  node-feature-rules).
- Firmware: fw_names[] in drivers/accel/ivpu/ivpu_fw.c at tag v6.19 asks only for
  intel/vpu/vpu_60xx_v1.bin (no _v0.0). Neither linux-firmware tag 20260916
  (WHENCE) nor intel/linux-npu-driver v1.38.0 (firmware/bin) ships it.
- A failed probe leaves no driver link and no accel node: ivpu_fw.c returns the
  request_firmware error from probe.

Derived from tests/fixtures/pantherlake with the iGPU and IAA removed. Not from
hardware: the CPU tree (pantherlake's), the kernel release string, the BDF.
